{
  "_comment": "Viewer settings. Layers come from the point cloud (data/lidar_points.json, written by site-model/houdini/tools/pack_wide.py) and from the design files; this file only gives display names, order, default visibility and colours. Unknown layers still appear under their own name (grey). Design files site-model/exports/design_<name>.glb load on top of the point cloud (listed in assets/models.json); their layers default to the Design style, visible. Camera values are three.js coordinates: x = east, y = up (m, NAVD88), z = -north, from the site origin E 384580 / N 3768520.",
  "designs": "assets/models.json",
  "time": {
    "_comment": "The Time module (user, 2026-10-13): buildings by the year they were built, each rising from the ground over the buildYears before it, with a soft front (front: its depth, as a share of the building's height). Buildings and landmarks turn white and opaque and stay; the rest goes to contextGrey at contextOpacity; the unbuilt towers keep their colour. undatedDim: the white of buildings with no year.",
    "opening": true,
    "undatedDim": 0.55,
    "buildYears": 5,
    "front": 0.25,
    "contextGrey": 0.45,
    "contextOpacity": 0.35,
    "groundFill": {
      "_comment": "ESTIMATED ground under the buildings, where the LiDAR saw only roofs (drawn as ground, in every mode): cellM grid, density = the mean of the ground cells within radiusM.",
      "cellM": 2,
      "radiusM": 20
    },
    "labels": {
      "_comment": "Labels on the buildings going up (blob-tracking frames): at most max new ones at once, the tallest first, for named buildings and landmarks (namedOnly) at least minHeightM tall; a labelled building keeps its frame and text once built, fading over fadeYears to doneOpacity; a text with no free place hides; one that could not get a label is still eligible holdYears after completion; unbuilt towers always.",
      "max": 6,
      "doneOpacity": 0.45,
      "namedOnly": true,
      "fadeYears": 8,
      "holdYears": 2,
      "minHeightM": 25
    },
    "cinema": {
      "_comment": "After the opening, if the camera was not touched: a loop of shots (wide orbit, cut to a hero tower filmed low and close, fly back out, crane down onto Y-1 ...). shotS / blendS seconds; heroes = the tallest labelled towers within heroWithinM of Y-1; labelOpacity = every label while filming (the hero full). on false = stop at the end.",
      "on": true,
      "shotS": 10,
      "blendS": 3.5,
      "heroes": 4,
      "heroWithinM": 700,
      "wideR": 1300,
      "wideTilt": 46,
      "labelOpacity": 0.3
    },
    "tour": {
      "_comment": "The camera while it plays from 1867 (the viewer's opening; opening false = start on today): it ends far out, on the whole site. turnDeg round the site, distance r0 -> r1 (m) and tilt0 -> tilt1 (degrees from straight down), about target.",
      "turnDeg": 220,
      "r0": 420,
      "r1": 1300,
      "tilt0": 64,
      "tilt1": 46,
      "target": [0, 95, 0]
    }
  },
  "ghosts": {
    "data": "data/ghosts.json",
    "_comment": "Unbuilt schemes on Y-1 (user, 2026-10-13), from site-model/ghosts/build_angels_landing.py: each tower's points are scattered at random over its walls and roof, as dense as the towers around Y-1 (ghosts.json density, measured by the script), and join the point cloud when it loads, as the estimated facades do: the same point size, thinning with distance and highlight as every building; their own layer (Unbuilt) and colour. inBands of the wall points lie within bandM of a floor line, the rest anywhere on the wall (as the estimated facades: 0.8, 0.25 m), so the storeys show; seed: the same scatter every time.",
    "inBands": 0.8,
    "bandM": 0.25,
    "seed": 11
