  "_landmarks": "The Landmarks layer by landmarkRule (user, 2026-10-10, option A, 1 km). One entry per monument; parts: one object name of each entity it covers (a monument outline that covers at least half of an entity's footprint takes that entity), which does not change when auto_entities.py renumbers the automatic entities. name is shown for automatic entities (named by their address) and where rename is set. built / builtSource: the building's own year, looked up 2026-10-10 (the assessor's year built is often a later remodel: Bradbury 1922 for 1893); a landmark without one shows no year. use replaces a wrong assessor use (Central Library: a parking-lot parcel). Every other entity draws as Buildings, also the Pershing Square Metro canopy (a hand-modelled part, not a landmark)."
